  "boxes": [
    {
      "type": "anchorbox",
      "title": "Consistency is the Cure",
      "description": "Just as studying requires daily effort, maintaining mental health and overcoming life's pains (Peera) requires constant (Nirantara), disciplined practice. You cannot cram for character; it must be built consistently over time.",
      "motivating_text": "",
      "citation": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "gotchabox",
      "items": [
        "The ड → र Shift: The Sanskrit word for pain is पीडा (Peedaa). Over time, the retroflex 'D' softens into a rolling 'R' sound, giving the beautiful Awadhi word पीरा (Peeraa).",
        "Verbs ending in -ai: Just like गावैं and लहै, the verbs नासै (Destroy) and हरै (Remove) are standard present-tense conjugations in Awadhi poetry."
      ]
    }
  ]
